Subject: [PATCH 2/4] C14, patch 2 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M20): THE
 README SPEAKS NO INNER LANGUAGE, AND POINTS TO THE WORKING RECORD AND ITS TWO
 INDICES AS SUCH

The README had seven of the inner words, in six places. It has none now, and the gate holds it at zero.

  - The line on the principle is main's sentence: the principle is a postulate, stated and not derived, as are
    the other two assumptions of the foundation's first layer; its wording is fixed in GENESIS, version 1.5.
  - The line on verification is main's sentence: every check is internal to the project (re-derivation,
    scripts run again, readings by separate sessions that did not write the work), and no outside review has
    taken place. One sentence is added: where a result is called checked, it says by which of these.
  - The register's line, in its generator (scripts/views/generate.py), not in its output: "queued work, leads,
    and questions not yet decided".
  - The plan's line: "the order of work chosen on 2026-10-30".
  - The line on how work is done: several sessions compute in parallel; what the record takes in from them is
    checked first and recorded, in two ledgers that are part of the working record.
  - The status page and the register are marked as the working record where the README sends a reader to them.
  - A new line names the working record and points to the verdict ledger and the spine as working indices that
    quote every verdict line word for word; their quotations are not rewritten.

TWO OF MAIN'S TESTS held the old sentences: tests/test_b1460_genesis_v1_5.py (the line on the principle) and
tests/test_readme_front_door.py (the line on verification). Each holds the same requirement in the new words,
under a dated note that keeps the line as it stood.

Every gate passes but the count of landings; the gates that read the README (the framing, the sweep of
retracted phrases, the pretense phrases, the facts of the front pages, the citations) pass. The test files that
read the README: all pass but the paper's manifest test, which failed from C13's patch 4 as first sent and
passes with its correction. Not checked by main.
